      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your pain is valid because your grief is real, and the feeling that \"finding yourself\" is a task you can't complete until he's back is a harsh truth that needs to be honored. Often, reconstructing a self after such a profound bond isn't about discovering a hidden version of you, but rather learning to stand alone while the other half is still gone. This waiting period is nothing to be afraid of, as it simply marks where your future spirit begins even if it still feels like a shell right now.",
      "source": "target",
